fix: dark-mode contrast on detail/create/edit cards + cleaner hero

EventDetailView, CreateEventView, and EditEventView had hardcoded
`background: white` on their section/info/sidebar cards which made
text unreadable in dark mode (white-on-near-white). Switched all
four card backgrounds to var(--surface) so they pick up the dark
surface token in dark mode.

Also tighten the hero to match the design reference:
- Remove three blurred coral/purple/blue glow blobs that produced a
  brown haze behind the hero copy in dark mode
- "happening" gradient: 3-stop coral->pink->mustard -> 2-stop
  oklch(0.63 0.20 22) -> oklch(0.72 0.18 40) (red->orange) per ref
- Browse Events / btn-primary (Sign Up): solid var(--primary) with
  coral glow, replacing the coral->pink gradient that read as salmon
- Stat numbers (6+, 1,200+, 40+): solid var(--primary), weight 800
- Body radial alpha 0.10 -> 0.05 to soften background wash
